e-burst is timing-nondeterministic.","The plan instead generalizes the CLI write-burst test test_cli_show_complete_or_erroring_under_write_burst (test_show_no_stall.py:112-142), whose contention is incidental: whether any read catches a lock held by a concurrent background push is a race with no synchronization primitive.","ensure_fresh reconverge uses lock_timeout=_RECONVERGE_LOCK_TIMEOUT (reads.py:257); reverting it to 15 (sync.py:54 _SYNC_LOCK_TIMEOUT=15) only stalls a read that actually overlaps a held lock — not guaranteed on any given burst round.","Mitigating: ed2b was empirically reproduced 8/8 during the contention window (ticket ed2b description), and the plan hedges 'on at least one surface' over 6 rounds x 4 surfaces, which raises overlap odds."],"finding":"The RED demonstration relies on incidental timing (a background push happening to hold the write lock during a read's reconverge window), not a deterministic lock-holder — so a green RED run under the reverted ledge could be a false negative (the ledge appears not to matter) rather than proof the property catches the regression.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f086e70c4a4e43c94","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Testing' section + Acceptance Criteria line 4 ('RED demonstrated by locally reverting the reads.py lock-timeout ledge')","norm_id":"n519026fd049b8bb9","priority":0.165,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["Author reverts the ledge, the burst happens not to overlap a held lock on any surface, the property stays green, and the author wrongly concludes the ledge is unnecessary (or that the test doesn't actually pin the invariant)."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan's 'Run every surface with --output json' instruction is incorrect for the `search` surface: `_cmd_search` never parses `--output` and rejects any unrecognized dashed arg with exit 2, so `rebar search <query> --output json` returns a nonzero exit — which the plan's own invariant classifies as an acceptable loud failure. The search surface's output-integrity assertion would therefore NEVER execute (it passes hollowly on every run, including the RED reverted-ledge tree), defeating the generic property for a named target surface. search emits JSON by DEFAULT (no flag), unlike show/list/ready which accept `--output json`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd5e5bd57266bd5dd","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'Run every surface with `--output json`'; Acceptance Criteria line 1 & 2","norm_id":"n50f9945115b77761","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Parameterize each surface with its own arg tuple and expected shape, e.g. show=(['show', tid], object), list=(['list','--output','json'], list), ready=(['ready','--output','json'], list), search=(['search', <query>], list) — note search takes NO --output flag. Add an assertion (or design the RED demo) that each surface produces at least one exit-0 invocation so a rejected-flag exit-2 can't hollowly pass.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan prescribes running every read surface — including `search` — with `--output json`, but the `search` subcommand does not accept a `--output`/`-o` flag: `_cmd_search` parses no output flag and rejects any `-`-prefixed arg outside its filter set with exit 2 (it always emits a JSON array by default). So `rebar search <query> --output json` exits 2, not JSON. Combined with the plan's rule that nonzero exits pass ('LOUD nonzero exit is acceptable' / assert-JSON only on exit 0), the search parameterization would exit 2 and pass VACUOUSLY, never exercising search's reconverge/output path — silently dropping the very surface the property exists to cover.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe5753638afaa3f9e","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Run every surface with `--output j